course: dictionary
lesson: 10624
title: The prefix un-
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unfinished is made of two parts: un- and finished. The little part at the front, un-, means not. Finished means done, so unfinished means not done yet.
explain: Read this sentence: «The painting is still unfinished, so the artist keeps working on it.» Ask yourself: what would fit in place of unfinished? "Not done yet" fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: Unfinished can also mean a problem that is still open. In a story, «the mind keeps bringing it back because it is unfinished business» tells you the secret keeps coming back to the mind because it has not been dealt with. Unfinished business is a job or problem that still needs sorting out.
fact: Unfinished means not finished, not complete yet.
fact: The prefix un- means not, and finished means done, so unfinished means not done.
fact: Unfinished wood or furniture has no paint or varnish on it, so it is bare and rough.
fact: «Unfinished business» means a problem or job that still needs to be dealt with.
fact: In school, «unfinished work» may be done as homework or at break time.
exercise: «The cake is still unfinished, because the icing is missing.» What does unfinished mean here? | Shared with everyone | Very tasty | *Not complete yet | Burnt and cold
exercise: Mia has «unfinished work» from school. What does that mean? | Work with lots of pictures | Work she has already handed in | *Work that is not done yet | Work that is too hard for anyone
exercise: Look at the word unfinished. What does the un- at the front mean? | Very | Before | Again | *Not
test: «The old table was unfinished wood, bare and rough with no paint on it.» What does unfinished mean in this sentence? | Broken into pieces | *Has no paint or varnish on it yet | Very cold to touch | Painted in bright colours
test: «He had some unfinished business with his brother after the argument.» What is unfinished business? | A game they had not started | A birthday they forgot | *A problem that still needs dealing with | A letter he had sent
exam: What is the opposite of unfinished? | *Finished | Unfinished | Finishing | Unfriendly
